{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'gap|connect|curve|series|caption|title|tooltip|legend|format|unit|keyboard|css' apps/docs/pages/{options,bar,getting-started}.md | head -116\"","aggregated_output":"apps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:15:The package has no runtime dependencies. Its module build comes in two flavours, chosen by the `development` export condition: a bundler that resolves that condition gets the development build, which also prints hints; otherwise you get the production build, which prints errors and warnings only. The styles need no import: the library adopts its stylesheet as a constructed style sheet, or, where that is not possible, adds a `<style>` element. A page that prefers to load the stylesheet itself can link `axylo/axylo.css`, and the library then uses that copy. The packed packages are tested in Chrome under a Content Security Policy without `unsafe-inline`, with the stylesheet adopted and with it linked (`tests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts`).\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:31:Point at a chart, or press Tab to reach its plot and use the arrow keys, or open its table. The only required options are `data` and the fields: `x` and `y` (and `series` for long rows), or `label` and `value` for a donut. `title` is not required, but without it (or `labelledBy`) the chart gets a generated name and warning [AX140](diagnostics.md#ax140).\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:50:4. **A day with no data.** When you know a day is missing, send it, with `sessions: null`. Axylo can infer a missing day only between two rows of a series that has at least three rows at a regular step, and never before the first row or after the last; with two rows, or an irregular series, the line runs straight across the missing day. See [missing values](data.md#missing-values).\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:57:| Name and summary | `title` is the visible heading and the chart's accessible name. In a card that already has a heading, `labelledBy` names the chart with it. The chart's description is a generated summary: chart type, series, the x range with its time zone, the value range, each series' minimum, maximum and last value, and anything left out. `description` adds to it. |\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:59:| Keyboard | Up to two tab stops while the table is closed: the plot, where the arrow keys move through the points and its value text describes the point in focus, and the toolbar, when the chart has controls. A compact chart has none. See [the keyboard map](accessibility.md#the-keyboard-map). |\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:60:| Reading values | Pointing in the plot shows what is there, by the chart type's rule (nearest x for line and area, the band for bars, the nearest point within 24 px for scatter, the slice for a donut). The tooltip sits against the marks it describes, not at the pointer, and lets the pointer through; rest on a point to move onto its tooltip, click to pin it. In a small plot the same text goes in a strip under the plot. Escape closes it. See [reading values with a pointer](accessibility.md#reading-values-with-a-pointer). |\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:61:| Colour and more than colour | Eight default colours that work in light and dark pages. Lines and areas also carry marker shapes, repeated in the legend and tooltip; bars take fill patterns past the eighth series. |\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:73:**1. Read the diagnostics.** Open the browser console. Every problem Axylo found is printed once per code per page as `[axylo AX…] \"Chart title\": what is wrong, where, and how to fix it`. The same list is on the chart as `chart.diagnostics`, current as soon as the call returns. Each code has a page under [Diagnostics](diagnostics.md). Hints, which are advice rather than problems, print in the development build only.\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:75:**2. Check which kind of x Axylo read.** A date off by one day almost always means instants where calendar dates were meant (item 1 above). If the tooltip heading names a time zone, Axylo read instants. If the x labels are your strings in input order, it read categories.\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:82:const problems = validate('line', { title: 'Monthly visitors', data: rows, x: 'month', y: 'visitors' });\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:17:bar(target, { data, x, y, series, layout: 'grouped', horizontal: false, ...options });\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:23:| `y`, `series` | One value field (with `series` for long rows), or a list of fields. Several series make groups. |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:24:| `layout` | `'grouped'` (default) puts the series side by side; `'stacked'` stacks them. |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:29:| Common options | `title`, `labelledBy`, `subtitle`, `description`, `state`, `legend`, `tooltip`, `table`, `colors`, `messages`, `locale`, `strict`, `onDiagnostic`. |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:37:| Pointer | The band under the pointer: the whole category, not only the bar. The tooltip lists every series in that category; a click pins it. See [reading values with a pointer](accessibility.md#reading-values-with-a-pointer). |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:38:| Keyboard | By category, then series. |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:41:| Missing values | A missing bar (a `null` or absent value, or a step Axylo infers is missing) gets a small \"no data\" mark, distinct from a zero bar: at the baseline for grouped bars, at the edge of the stack for stacked ones. A slot a series simply has no row for, as for a weekly series beside daily ones, gets no bar and no mark. |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:42:| Stacking | Positive parts stack up from zero, negative parts down from it, and the axis covers both. With mixed signs each bar shows two totals, of its positive and of its negative parts, and the readout names both (\"Total 165 k USD and -60 k USD\" in the example below); the bar does not show their difference. A missing part has zero height and the total is marked \"incomplete\"; a part is missing whenever its series has no value at that x, also when the series simply has no row there. |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:43:| Long labels | Remedies in order: thinning (date, number and `ordered` category axes only), wrapping to three lines, rotating up to 45°, truncating in the middle with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, the chart says \"Some labels hidden. See table.\" and [AX143](diagnostics.md#ax143) suggests `horizontal: true`. Axylo never switches orientation by itself: that would change what the chart says at a glance. |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:45:| Many series | Colour and fill pattern: from the ninth series bars get patterns, which gives 32 distinct combinations before they repeat; warning [AX130](diagnostics.md#ax130) from the ninth. A [compact](compact.md) bar chart, which has no legend, gives neighbouring series different patterns from the second series on. |\napps/docs/pages/bar.md:46:| Reference lines | Drawn and labelled, included in the automatic domain, listed in the summary and table caption. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:12:| [Encoding](#encoding-line-area-bar) (`x`, `y`, `series`) | yes | yes | yes | – | – |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:30:| `title` | `string \\| Title` | none | Visible heading and accessible name. Without it (and without `labelledBy`) the name is generated, with AX140. In a compact chart it is the accessible name only. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:31:| `labelledBy` | `string` | none | Id of an existing heading that names the chart, for cards that already show a title. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:32:| `subtitle` | `string` | none | A line under the title. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:35:| `legend` | `'auto' \\| false \\| 'top' \\| 'right' \\| 'bottom'` | `'auto'` | Where the legend goes, or `false` for none. `'auto'` places it under the plot. A chart with one series has no legend entries. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:36:| `tooltip` | `boolean` | `true` | The pointer readout: the tooltip, or in a small plot the strip under it. With `false` nothing is pinned, and a click still selects. Keyboard reading is not affected. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:38:| `colors` | `Readonly<Record<string, string>>` | none | A CSS colour per series key: the `series` value for long rows, the field name for wide rows, the slice label on a donut. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:44:### Title\napps/docs/pages/options.md:46:When `title` is an object:\napps/docs/pages/options.md:48:<!-- options: Title -->\napps/docs/pages/options.md:51:| `text` | `string` | required | The title. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:57:Long rows name one `y` and a `series`; wide rows give `y` as a list and no `series`. The two forms are exclusive. One series needs only a single `y`.\napps/docs/pages/options.md:63:| `y` | `ValueField<Row> \\| readonly ValueField<Row>[]` | required | The value field, or one field per series. See [Value fields](#value-fields). The first field sets the shared value axis's domain and scale. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:64:| `series` | `SeriesKey<Row>` | none | The field whose value names and keys each row's series (long rows only). |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:83:| `label` | `string` | required | Shown beside the line or band, and listed in the summary and the table caption. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:99:| `stacked` | `boolean` | `false` | Stack the series; the tooltip adds the total, or both totals when signs are mixed. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:106:| `layout` | `'grouped' \\| 'stacked'` | `'grouped'` | Several series side by side, or stacked. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:118:| `series` | `SeriesKey<Row>` | none | The field that groups points into series. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:125:| `label` | `SeriesKey<Row>` | required | The field that names, and keys, each slice. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:137:| `label` | `string` | the field name | Axis title, and the series name in tooltip, table and announcements. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:138:| `unit` | `string` | none | Follows values in tooltip, table and announcements: `'ms'`, `'USD'`. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:140:| `format` | `Intl.NumberFormatOptions \\| ((value: number) => string)` | the locale's grouping, the full integer part and up to six significant fraction digits | How values are written in tooltip, table and announcements. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:141:| `tickFormat` | `Intl.NumberFormatOptions \\| ((value: number) => string)` | the locale's grouping, with the step's fraction digits; compact from a largest tick of one million, scientific from 10¹⁵ | How axis ticks are written. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:142:| `missing` | `'gap' \\| 'zero'` | `'gap'` | What a missing value means. `'zero'` is for counts where absence means none. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:156:| `label` | `string` | the field name | Axis title of a number axis; a date, time or category axis is titled only when you give one. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:157:| `unit` | `string` | none | Follows x values in tooltip, table and announcements. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:158:| `format` | `Intl.DateTimeFormatOptions \\| Intl.NumberFormatOptions \\| ((value: XValue) => string)` | from the kind of x | How x values are written in tooltip, table and announcements. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:159:| `tickFormat` | `Intl.DateTimeFormatOptions \\| Intl.NumberFormatOptions \\| ((value: XValue) => string)` | from the kind of x | How x ticks are written. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:171:| `unit` | `string` | none | As above. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:172:| `format` | `Intl.DateTimeFormatOptions \\| Intl.NumberFormatOptions \\| ((value: XValue) => string)` | from the kind of x | As above. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:173:| `tickFormat` | `Intl.DateTimeFormatOptions \\| Intl.NumberFormatOptions \\| ((value: XValue) => string)` | from the kind of x | As above. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:202:| `hover` | `Point<Row> \\| null` | The datum under the pointer or the keyboard's point; `null` when nothing is picked. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:209:| `series` | `string` | The series key: the `series` value for long rows, the field name for wide rows, the slice label on a donut. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:223:| `chart` | `string` | The chart's title, else its element id. |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:230:`validate(type, options)` takes `'line'`, `'area'`, `'bar'`, `'scatter'` or `'donut'` and that type's options, runs the checks a created chart runs from its call without a DOM, and returns `Diagnostic[]`. It cannot find what needs a page: contrast, sizes, label fitting, formatters, or whether a `labelledBy` id exists. See [Diagnostics](diagnostics.md#validate-in-node-and-in-tests).\napps/docs/pages/options.md:244:There is no `width`, `height`, `responsive`, `theme`, `palette` or `animation` option. Size comes from the container, colours from [CSS](theming.md), and motion from the reader's settings: the first render is not animated, and nothing moves under reduced motion. Each of these names, like any unknown key, is ignored with [AX150](diagnostics.md#ax150), which suggests the closest known option.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
