{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'DX12|DX12/' acceptance/report.md | cut -c1-400 | head -15 && nl -ba rehearsal/run.mjs | tail -38 && nl -ba apps/docs/pages/data.md | rg 'The fix|Missing values|Numbers sent as strings|Order and duplicates|With TypeScript'\"","aggregated_output":"131:| DX12 | Given fixed prompts and trap fixtures (UTC-midnight ISO dates, numeric strings, unsorted rows, missing days, a misspelled field), a coding agent with only the published docs makes a first chart with no error diagnostics that passes the reader criteria; recorded as agent rehearsal, not as user evidence. | not run | not run | not run | not run | not run | not run |\n310:- **DX12** · line, area, bar, scatter, donut, compact · Not done yet: the scripted agent rehearsal has not been run (STATUS.md, next actions, 2026-11-18), and the repository holds no rehearsal script, prompt set or trap fixtures for the rehearsal (the documentation's examples cover dates, missing data, numeric strings and unsorted input, but they are not the rehearsal's traps). When it is run,\n    45\t  const [audit, observed] = await Promise.all([auditTranscript(log, workspace), observeAgent(agent, log)]);\n    46\t  const record = await reserveRecord(start.toISOString().slice(0, 10), agent, task);\n    47\t  await copyFile(transcript, join(record, 'transcript.jsonl'));\n    48\t  await copyFile(stderr, join(record, 'stderr.log'));\n    49\t\n    50\t  const answer = join(workspace, 'chart.js');\n    51\t  const answerStat = await lstat(answer).catch(error => {\n    52\t    if (error.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error;\n    53\t  });\n    54\t  if (answerStat?.isFile()) await copyFile(answer, join(record, 'chart.js'));\n    55\t  let result;\n    56\t  try {\n    57\t    result = await grade(workspace, task);\n    58\t  } catch (error) {\n    59\t    result = { pass: false, criteria: [{ name: 'grader', pass: false, detail: String(error) }], diagnostics: [], timezones: [] };\n    60\t    await writeJson(join(workspace, 'grade.json'), result);\n    61\t  }\n    62\t  await copyFile(join(workspace, 'grade.json'), join(record, 'grade.json'));\n    63\t  await writeJson(join(record, 'run.json'), {\n    64\t    kind: 'agent rehearsal', agent, task, requested: { model, effort: effort ?? null }, observed,\n    65\t    startedAt: start.toISOString(), endedAt: end.toISOString(), durationMs: end - start,\n    66\t    timeoutMs, exit, ...audit,\n    67\t  });\n    68\t  const agentFailed = exit.code !== 0 || exit.timedOut || exit.error !== null;\n    69\t  const status = audit.void ? 'void' : agentFailed || !result.pass ? 'fail' : 'pass';\n    70\t  console.log(`Agent rehearsal: ${status}. Record: ${record}`);\n    71\t  process.exitCode = exit.error || result.criteria.some(item => ['browser', 'grader'].includes(item.name)) ? 2\n    72\t    : status === 'pass' ? 0 : 1;\n    73\t}\n    74\t\n    75\tif (isMain(import.meta.url)) {\n    76\t  try {\n    77\t    await main();\n    78\t  } catch (error) {\n    79\t    console.error(String(error));\n    80\t    process.exitCode = 2;\n    81\t  }\n    82\t}\n    47\tWith TypeScript, field names are checked against your row type. A misspelled field, a text field on a value axis, or wide `y` together with `series` does not compile. With untyped rows (from `fetch().json()`, say) the same mistakes are reported at run time: a field that no row has is [AX101](diagnostics.md#ax101), and the message lists the keys the rows do have and, when one is close, the closest match. With no rows, there is nothing to check a field against, and nothing is reported.\n    67\tAxylo notices at least two distinct instants that all fall at the same time of day, whole days apart, and raises hint [AX111](diagnostics.md#ax111). The fix is one of:\n    91\t## Missing values\n   118\t## Numbers sent as strings\n   129\t## Order and duplicates\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
